## Complementarity and dependence

Fig3 measures completed H2 amounts by GC in the coupled ferredoxin/hydrogenase
system. Caption coefficients1.1NAD+/H2 and2.2NADPH/H2 imply approximate reciprocal
ratios0.9091 and0.4545, and ratio2 under the supported coupling interpretation.
They are not90.9%/45.45% assay-validity grades. Serial gas samples are time points,
not independent enzyme preparations; graph/caption repeats are one experiment.

Fig4 uses the net NADP+reduced minus NADHoxidized endpoint in the opposite
direction. It addresses stoichiometry under its own conditions, not replication
of the backward8 U/mg rate. The two28 U/mg donor rows concern the coupled forward
reaction; row count or equal values alone establishes neither independent
replication nor exact duplicated measurements. Between-batch reproducibility
is reported for stoichiometry, with no numerical count/dispersion that can be
